# What never goes into the build context.
#
# Without this file the context is about four gigabytes and almost none of it is wanted: .tools holds the
# vendored PostgreSQL and PostGIS archives at 1.58 GB, .venv holds a Windows virtualenv at 1.54 GB that
# cannot run in a Linux image anyway, node_modules is 443 MB the API never imports, and apps/web/.next is
# 289 MB of build output. Docker sends the context to the daemon before reading the first instruction, so
# an ignored file is not merely unused, it is transferred and then discarded.
#
# Written in the same commit as infra/Dockerfile.api. A Dockerfile whose build takes ten minutes to send
# nothing useful is a Dockerfile people stop using.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environments and caches. The Linux image builds its own virtualenv.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node. The API image runs no JavaScript.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/out/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored binaries and local runtime state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.tools/
var/
mlruns/
artifacts/
*.log

# The raw corpus is content addressed object storage. In production it lives in S3 or R2, which is what
# AUSPICE_RAW_BACKEND=s3 selects, so a local copy has no reason to be in the image.
data/raw/
data/derived/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Belt and braces: these are gitignored too, but a build context is not a git tree and an
# accidental .env in the image is a credential in a layer that anyone who can pull it can read.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.kiro/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# History and tooling that has no bearing on the runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.agent/
tests/
AUSPICE_Master_Spec.md
AUSPICE_BUILD_PROMPT.md
AUDIT_REPORT.md
bootstrap.log
